WEBVTT

00:00:07.917 --> 00:00:14.208
Antimatter: A mere 0.1 gram puts off
as much energy as an atomic bomb.

00:00:14.208 --> 00:00:17.542
Yanagisawa's research
had enabled continuous generation

00:00:17.542 --> 00:00:23.750
by splicing the antimatter particle
acceleration cycle into a living being.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.167
Legendary assassin the Reaper spent his days

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:29.833
undergoing these experiments.

00:00:29.833 --> 00:00:33.208
The antimatter energy that had
begun circulating within his body

00:00:33.208 --> 00:00:39.208
had replaced his body tissue
with tough and flexible structures.

00:00:39.208 --> 00:00:42.417
Yanagisawa called them "tentacles,"
and, fearing them,

00:00:42.417 --> 00:00:44.625
reinforced the restraint table

00:00:44.625 --> 00:00:49.000
and left the dangerous monitoring
entirely to Aguri Yukimura.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.667
And so she knew.

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:54.042
She knew the Reaper
knew neither his real name

00:00:54.042 --> 00:00:56.583
nor the day he was born,

00:00:56.583 --> 00:01:02.042
and that his kind words and smiles
were studied--as means to a kill.

00:01:02.042 --> 00:01:03.958
And <i>he </i>knew.

00:01:03.958 --> 00:01:09.583
He knew there was no love
between her and her fiancé, Yanagisawa,

00:01:09.583 --> 00:01:13.875
and that she had a little sister,
a keen actor, of whom she was proud.

00:01:13.875 --> 00:01:17.292
It had already been nearly
a year since the two had met.

00:01:17.292 --> 00:01:22.750
Along the way, this room had
become a space for them to chat.

00:01:27.958 --> 00:01:31.958
"16th Period: Past Time"
"by Hinano Kurahashi"

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:37.792
Oh, right! Check out the new
undershirt I bought today!

00:01:37.792 --> 00:01:39.500
You never learn, do you.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:42.542
No sense dragging down womankind
with your tasteless clothes.

00:01:42.542 --> 00:01:46.125
Ta-da! An ogre-patterned tube top!

00:01:46.125 --> 00:01:49.958
It's a tad tight, but way stylish, right?

00:01:55.083 --> 00:01:56.417
Um...

00:01:56.417 --> 00:01:58.708
I knew it. It's weird.

00:01:58.708 --> 00:02:01.292
--I just thought it was cute, so--
--No, no! This is, uh...

00:02:01.292 --> 00:02:04.708
Could the experiments be doing this?

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:07.708
Some honest tentacles you have there.

00:02:07.708 --> 00:02:08.792
Huh?

00:02:08.792 --> 00:02:11.292
The way those hands can take on any shape--

00:02:11.292 --> 00:02:15.000
they might just reflect
who you yourself would like to be.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.375
Me?

00:02:16.375 --> 00:02:19.708
Had you been born in a peaceful world,

00:02:19.708 --> 00:02:25.875
you'd've been smart, but slightly perverted,
a tad doofy, petty, headstrong,

00:02:25.875 --> 00:02:30.917
and able to pull off
an honest-to-goodness kind smile.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:39.750
Hey, Akari, I found some time
this evening. Want to grab dinner?

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:43.292
Never mind that--you sound so dang cheerful!

00:02:43.292 --> 00:02:45.125
Who's the new guy?

00:02:45.125 --> 00:02:48.292
Wh-What are you saying? I'm engaged!

00:02:48.292 --> 00:02:53.000
Oh, so what. Cut that
two-faced tyrant loose already.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:53.833
Listen here...

00:02:53.833 --> 00:02:58.375
But sure. I gotta hear about
this guy who's caught your eye.

00:02:58.375 --> 00:02:59.375
So we're on?

00:02:59.375 --> 00:03:00.917
Yup! Your treat!

00:03:00.917 --> 00:03:02.333
Sheesh...

00:03:03.958 --> 00:03:05.625
A present?

00:03:05.625 --> 00:03:09.125
Uh-huh. You were saying your neck was cold.

00:03:09.125 --> 00:03:12.667
This covers a good-sized area,
and it's snazzy, too.

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:13.833
Uh, thanks.

00:03:13.833 --> 00:03:16.333
I see you find it unsatisfactory.

00:03:16.333 --> 00:03:21.083
No, it's just... why a present out of the blue?

00:03:21.083 --> 00:03:24.583
Today marks a year since I met you.

00:03:24.583 --> 00:03:29.542
If you don't know the day
you were born, why not make it today?

00:03:30.417 --> 00:03:35.792
You've lent me your ear so many times
and given me so much advice.

00:03:35.792 --> 00:03:40.250
As my thanks for meeting you,
please let me give you a birthday.

00:03:42.458 --> 00:03:44.792
I'll take it.

00:03:44.792 --> 00:03:47.083
Wonderful!

00:03:47.083 --> 00:03:50.000
But I guess I can't give you <i>this</i>, huh.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:54.250
Not as long as this wall's here. And...

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:59.333
Yanagisawa wants me to quit
my teaching job to work here full-time.

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:02.250
The students in my last E Class...

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:08.042
I never did manage to
put that spark in their eyes after all.

00:04:08.042 --> 00:04:15.708
I'm still too green
for these new kids... and yet...

00:04:15.708 --> 00:04:19.625
But my students really are all good kids!

00:04:19.625 --> 00:04:24.167
All so unique, and earnest, and genuine!

00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:30.167
And that's why I want that job, to help them.

00:04:30.167 --> 00:04:32.542
Because I like them all...

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.292
Mr. Reaper...

00:04:36.292 --> 00:04:38.542
I want to touch you.

00:04:38.542 --> 00:04:40.958
You've been my rock.

00:04:40.958 --> 00:04:46.167
I want you to give me the strength
to hang in there this final year...

00:04:56.833 --> 00:05:02.792
Before he knew it, his false smile
had become the real thing.

00:05:15.917 --> 00:05:19.958
It's all right. You can do it.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:23.292
Yeah.

00:05:23.292 --> 00:05:26.292
The first time they touched

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:30.292
was three hours before
the crescent moon came to be.

00:05:51.792 --> 00:05:53.083
The moon?!

00:05:53.083 --> 00:05:56.250
Yes--70 percent destroyed!

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:58.708
A lab rat on the lunar surface
experienced a discharge

00:05:58.708 --> 00:06:00.375
of antimatter energy!

00:06:00.375 --> 00:06:04.250
So cell division exceeded natural limits, eh?

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:08.042
Calculate the day this same
phenomenon would occur in a human!

00:06:08.042 --> 00:06:09.458
Yes, sir!

00:06:10.833 --> 00:06:14.708
Got it: March 13 of next year!

00:06:14.708 --> 00:06:18.500
That's the day he<i> and</i>
the entire world will be destroyed.

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.292
What will we do, sir?

00:06:21.292 --> 00:06:22.833
Isn't it obvious?

00:06:22.833 --> 00:06:28.167
We put him down. Should be a cinch,
if we can just stop his heart.

00:06:28.167 --> 00:06:30.167
Notify our U.S. HQ at once!

00:06:30.167 --> 00:06:31.583
Yes, sir!

00:06:33.667 --> 00:06:38.083
Doomed to a cursed death. I had that coming.

00:06:38.083 --> 00:06:40.625
Don't give up hope!
There may be a way to save--

00:06:40.625 --> 00:06:45.083
But since I have this power and all...

00:06:45.958 --> 00:06:49.875
This is goodbye, Aguri.

00:06:49.875 --> 00:06:51.667
I'm leaving this place.

00:06:51.667 --> 00:06:56.250
A little earlier than planned,
but this much power is enough.

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:58.000
Enough for a place like this.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:02.125
No! No more evil! All this time, we--

00:07:02.125 --> 00:07:03.500
You'd stop me?

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:04.708
Yes!

00:07:04.708 --> 00:07:10.500
You? How? With those
arms of yours? That brain?

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:11.708
Huh?

00:07:11.708 --> 00:07:18.250
Unless your abilities transcend mine,
you can't stop me <i>or </i>save me.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:21.833
You're not even worth taking hostage.

00:07:21.833 --> 00:07:25.500
Now leave before you die a pointless death.

00:07:34.917 --> 00:07:39.958
It's Yukimura. Unlock door 1.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:51.333
Now to try out the powers
I've gained by putting up with torture!

00:07:56.083 --> 00:07:57.833
What happened to the security system?!

00:07:57.833 --> 00:07:59.833
I-It's not working!

00:07:59.833 --> 00:08:03.208
A powerful mucus is jamming the panels!

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:06.458
Much obliged, Yanagisawa.

00:08:06.458 --> 00:08:09.625
I have this invincible body, thanks to you--

00:08:09.625 --> 00:08:12.792
with some guidance from me, anyway.

00:08:13.708 --> 00:08:16.792
Is he saying he gamed the experiment?!

00:08:16.792 --> 00:08:20.167
Kotaro! You have to help him, or else--

00:08:20.167 --> 00:08:22.792
You <i>bitch</i>!

00:08:22.792 --> 00:08:24.667
Fawning on any man that comes along?

00:08:24.667 --> 00:08:26.417
That's my thanks for taking you in?

00:08:26.417 --> 00:08:29.750
Who do you think you are--you and him both?!

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:35.083
Dammit! Get the guards together
and intercept him!

00:08:40.625 --> 00:08:43.458
Don't push your luck, guinea pig.

00:08:43.458 --> 00:08:47.625
And don't think we were always
only about the experiments.

00:08:57.750 --> 00:08:59.625
Fire!

00:09:01.958 --> 00:09:05.833
If all you're after is a ruptured aorta...

00:09:05.833 --> 00:09:08.083
...a grain of sand will do the trick.

00:09:09.958 --> 00:09:13.250
I could have killed
the likes of you at any time.

00:09:17.208 --> 00:09:19.125
Tentacle mines!

00:09:19.125 --> 00:09:22.000
A byproduct of antimatter organisms...

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:24.250
Attach sensors to control them,

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:26.833
and they become weapons
attacking at subsonic speeds;

00:09:26.833 --> 00:09:31.750
transplanted into humans,
they grant superhuman battle powers!

00:09:35.208 --> 00:09:40.500
<i>This </i>isn't enough to do me in.

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:42.667
K-Kill him!

00:09:42.667 --> 00:09:45.458
Surround him! Exterminate him!

00:09:50.292 --> 00:09:52.542
Drop the reinforced acrylic!

00:10:30.333 --> 00:10:34.083
I'll die in a year regardless.

00:10:34.083 --> 00:10:37.208
I don't care if I die here.

00:10:37.208 --> 00:10:40.667
And I don't mind dying with the earth, either.

00:10:44.167 --> 00:10:45.750
No!

00:10:48.083 --> 00:10:52.583
If you go that way, there's...

00:10:52.583 --> 00:10:55.667
...there's no coming back!

00:10:55.667 --> 00:10:57.833
She had seen everything.

00:10:57.833 --> 00:11:01.042
Seen everything and was curious about it all.

00:11:01.042 --> 00:11:05.250
But her being there, seeing me...

00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:08.542
<i>That's </i>something I hadn't seen.

00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:20.167
Aguri!

00:11:27.042 --> 00:11:29.292
Now I've done it.

00:11:29.292 --> 00:11:33.333
Never thought that trap
would just slither out like that...

00:11:33.333 --> 00:11:34.708
Why...

00:11:34.708 --> 00:11:40.333
I had the feeling... my voice
wouldn't be enough to stop you...

00:11:40.333 --> 00:11:44.625
If I'd noticed 0.1 seconds faster,
I could have protected her.

00:11:44.625 --> 00:11:48.833
If I'd practiced using my tentacles to heal,
I could have saved her.

00:11:48.833 --> 00:11:53.042
Why, when I had plenty of time to notice...

00:11:53.042 --> 00:11:59.250
Why didn't I use my deadly,
destructive strength to help someone?

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:03.292
Why? Why?!

00:12:03.292 --> 00:12:08.167
I may as well have killed you myself.

00:12:08.167 --> 00:12:11.750
Of course... you didn't...

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:15.292
I just did... what I wanted to do...

00:12:15.292 --> 00:12:21.083
Besides... I don't mind being killed... for you.

00:12:21.083 --> 00:12:24.500
That's how important you are to me...

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:29.792
One day you, too,
will meet someone like that...

00:12:29.792 --> 00:12:32.833
If you were the one to kill me,
I'd have no regrets.

00:12:32.833 --> 00:12:37.042
But to think there could be
anyone else like you out there...

00:12:40.667 --> 00:12:44.958
In this year you have left...

00:12:44.958 --> 00:12:52.208
...if you would give your time...
go teach those children...

00:12:52.208 --> 00:12:59.000
Like you... they're wandering in the darkness...

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:03.583
If you look at them head-on, I'm sure...

00:13:06.625 --> 00:13:11.083
What splendid tentacles...

00:13:11.083 --> 00:13:20.417
With hands like these...
I'm sure you'll be a splendid teacher...

00:13:28.792 --> 00:13:41.750
<i>I want to keep listening to your story</i>
<i> </i>

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:44.000
<i>Just like this, forever</i>
<i>  </i>

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:46.708
<i>Just like this, forever</i>
So uncool.

00:13:46.708 --> 00:13:49.250
<i>Just like this, forever</i>
At long last, he realized:

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:54.083
<i>Just like this, forever</i>
Her faults were also part of her charm.

00:13:54.083 --> 00:14:01.083
<i>Though I know time changes everything</i>

00:14:01.083 --> 00:14:06.417
<i>Though I know time changes everything</i>
I'll use the time I have left to be a teacher.

00:14:06.417 --> 00:14:06.875
<i>Though I know time changes everything</i>
To keep looking, with my eyes,

00:14:06.875 --> 00:14:09.500
<i>I want to believe in something that won't go away</i>
To keep looking, with my eyes,

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:11.625
<i>I want to believe in something that won't go away</i>
at the students you've been watching.

00:14:11.625 --> 00:14:16.792
<i>I want to believe in something that won't go away</i>

00:14:16.792 --> 00:14:20.500
<i>I want to believe in something that won't go away</i>
I won't let go of your students, no matter what.

