<i>Spills from my eye</i>
I learned the fundamentals of being a teacher from her.

00:15:41.917 --> 00:15:42.833
<i>Blurring the moon's light</i>
I learned the fundamentals of being a teacher from her.

00:15:42.833 --> 00:15:45.625
<i>Blurring the moon's light</i>
I added my own knowledge and experience

00:15:45.625 --> 00:15:50.083
<i>Blurring the moon's light</i>
and prepared to face you all.

00:15:50.083 --> 00:15:52.375
<i>Blurring the moon's light</i>
I would use my abilities to the fullest

00:15:52.375 --> 00:15:53.917
<i>Blurring the moon's light</i>
to give you the gift of the best growth and development.

00:15:53.917 --> 00:15:55.875
to give you the gift of the best growth and development.

00:15:55.875 --> 00:15:59.750
But how best to do that?

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:03.667
I racked my brain...

00:16:03.667 --> 00:16:07.292
...and finally landed on
the assassination classroom,

00:16:07.292 --> 00:16:11.333
where I'd use what remained of my life.

00:16:11.333 --> 00:16:14.625
It had been nine months since
Koro Sensei came to the E Class.

00:16:14.625 --> 00:16:17.625
We'd all grown by leaps and bounds.

00:16:17.625 --> 00:16:22.875
He really is the best teacher we could have.

00:16:22.875 --> 00:16:25.500
After Koro Sensei had talked for a half hour

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:29.042
about the real reasons he'd become a teacher,

00:16:29.042 --> 00:16:35.083
our minds were instantly overrun
with memories of our time with him.

00:16:35.083 --> 00:16:37.042
The frightening times,

00:16:37.042 --> 00:16:38.917
the infuriating times,

00:16:38.917 --> 00:16:40.625
the happy times,

00:16:40.625 --> 00:16:42.292
the fun times,

00:16:42.292 --> 00:16:44.583
the fun times,

00:16:44.583 --> 00:16:46.875
the fun times...

00:16:47.833 --> 00:16:52.333
Now, for the first time, we realized

00:16:52.333 --> 00:16:56.542
the formidable challenge
we'd had foisted upon us.

00:16:57.625 --> 00:17:03.333
Do we have to <i>kill </i>this teacher of ours?

00:17:05.333 --> 00:17:08.917
Say, Karasuma...

00:17:08.917 --> 00:17:14.417
Do you really know what it means to kill?

00:17:14.917 --> 00:17:18.917
"Assassination Classroom, Final Season"
"by Nagisa Shiota"

00:17:20.250 --> 00:17:24.792
The explosion was set
for this coming March 13--

00:17:24.792 --> 00:17:29.583
strangely enough,
Kunugigaoka Junior High's graduation day.

00:17:30.583 --> 00:17:35.083
We rang in the new year. Now it's January 6.

00:17:35.083 --> 00:17:39.625
The number of students plotting
assassinations during winter break

00:17:39.625 --> 00:17:42.333
was precisely zero.

00:17:44.458 --> 00:17:46.833
How're you doing, Kaya--

00:17:46.833 --> 00:17:47.833
Miss Yukimura?

00:17:47.833 --> 00:17:51.792
You can call me "Kayano."
"Kaede Kayano" isn't bad at all.

00:17:51.792 --> 00:17:55.792
So much for your winter break, huh?
Not to mention the holidays.

00:17:55.792 --> 00:17:58.625
I'll make it back just in time for the new term.

00:17:58.625 --> 00:18:01.875
How was your time off?

00:18:01.875 --> 00:18:06.458
None of us could even bring up
the subject of assassination.

00:18:06.458 --> 00:18:09.667
I'm sorry. It's all my fault.

00:18:09.667 --> 00:18:14.500
Now that I know the truth,
I've gotten some closure, but...

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:18.167
Now the rest of you know
all about Koro Sensei's past.

00:18:18.167 --> 00:18:20.583
No, Kayano--

00:18:20.583 --> 00:18:23.875
we had to find out sometime.

00:18:23.875 --> 00:18:28.208
We all tried so hard not to face facts...

00:18:28.208 --> 00:18:32.625
...so we could enjoy our fun assassinations
for even just a little longer.

00:18:32.625 --> 00:18:36.458
Everyone's probably spent the break thinking

00:18:36.458 --> 00:18:40.208
how we can face our
assassination classroom from now on.

00:18:41.833 --> 00:18:45.625
Oh! And... I need to apologize
to you, Kayano. About that night.

00:18:45.625 --> 00:18:47.167
I'm sorry!

00:18:47.167 --> 00:18:51.083
That's the only thing I could
come up with in the heat of the moment.

00:18:53.125 --> 00:18:56.292
Are you mad?

00:18:56.292 --> 00:19:01.250
Heck, no! You saved me.
All I can do is thank you.

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:04.292
Thank goodness!
If you'd said we were through...

00:19:04.292 --> 00:19:08.750
You worry too much. We'll be friends forever.

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:12.750
We should get going.
Kayano must be tuckered out.

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:14.625
You're right.

00:19:14.625 --> 00:19:15.750
Bye, Kayano.

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:18.333
--See you in a couple days.
--Later!

00:19:18.333 --> 00:19:19.750
Uh-huh...

00:19:21.583 --> 00:19:23.750
What's up, Kanzaki?

00:19:23.750 --> 00:19:26.917
She'd been watching the class
from somewhat of a distance,

00:19:26.917 --> 00:19:30.333
but now I feel like she's finally
joined us in the same place.

00:19:34.792 --> 00:19:36.125
Why, that...

00:19:36.125 --> 00:19:40.167
That... was like being controlled,
personality and all!

00:19:40.167 --> 00:19:45.208
Now that I know about that...
how can I ever act again?

00:19:45.208 --> 00:19:48.875
Here I thought I was the
number-one assassin in our class.

00:19:48.875 --> 00:19:51.042
I don't know about my regular human body,

00:19:51.042 --> 00:19:53.958
but with my tentacles
and instantaneous firepower,

00:19:53.958 --> 00:19:57.292
no way could anyone best me as an assassin...

00:19:58.542 --> 00:20:00.167
And yet...

00:20:00.167 --> 00:20:05.125
...I got shot through the heart as easy as pie.

00:20:05.125 --> 00:20:07.208
I'm utterly defeated.

00:20:07.208 --> 00:20:13.458
There's no better assassin
in our class than Nagisa.

00:20:13.458 --> 00:20:18.375
I guess now...
I have to play the part of his friend.

00:20:20.208 --> 00:20:22.708
The third term is upon us, class--

00:20:22.708 --> 00:20:23.083
"3rd Term Begins! 64 Days Till the Earth's Destruction! Nurufufufu!"
The third term is upon us, class--

00:20:23.083 --> 00:20:26.167
"3rd Term Begins! 64 Days Till the Earth's Destruction! Nurufufufu!"
let's play hard and kill hard this year, too.

00:20:29.875 --> 00:20:31.542
"Staff Room"

00:20:31.542 --> 00:20:34.292
"Staff Room"
You must have known this would happen,

00:20:34.292 --> 00:20:37.167
that they'd be like this.

00:20:37.167 --> 00:20:41.250
Especially now, with the
heavy burden you've put on them--

00:20:41.250 --> 00:20:44.917
can you really carry out your duties as a teacher?

00:20:44.917 --> 00:20:46.250
"Staff Room"

00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:50.500
"Staff Room"
If I weren't prepared to be flexible as the situation demanded,

00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:54.250
"Staff Room"
I wouldn't have become a teacher in the first place.

00:20:56.875 --> 00:20:59.542
The most foolish kill

00:20:59.542 --> 00:21:03.417
is to kill recklessly, out of emotion or greed.

00:21:03.417 --> 00:21:06.083
That's what animals do.

00:21:06.083 --> 00:21:07.625
Professor Bitch...

00:21:07.625 --> 00:21:14.125
Next is to kill your feelings
while you kill your target,

00:21:14.125 --> 00:21:17.667
giving up so very much
in exchange for a bounty.

00:21:17.667 --> 00:21:20.000
Like I did.

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:23.500
You really need to think this through, kids,

00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:28.250
so you won't kill off
the feelings you hold most dear.

00:21:31.917 --> 00:21:34.875
"3rd Term Begins! 64 Days Till
the Earth's Destruction! Nurufufufu!" "Boom"

00:21:34.875 --> 00:21:36.375
So... what?

00:21:36.375 --> 00:21:41.500
It ain't like you to be callin' us
all together like this, Nagisa.

00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:43.875
There's something I'd really like to discuss.

00:21:43.875 --> 00:21:46.333
What is it?

00:21:46.333 --> 00:21:50.083
I don't know if it's even possible,

00:21:50.083 --> 00:21:54.708
but I want to find a way
to save Koro Sensei's life.

00:21:56.542 --> 00:22:07.500
<i>The memories I've arranged</i>
<i>little by little keep me warm</i>

00:22:07.500 --> 00:22:19.042
<i>A small room, hearts connecting:</i>
<i>you taught me gently</i>

00:22:19.042 --> 00:22:31.792
<i>Once this season comes for me, I won't be able</i>

00:22:31.792 --> 00:22:37.042
<i>To search out your figure anymore</i>

00:22:37.042 --> 00:22:42.792
<i>I'll never forget</i>

00:22:42.792 --> 00:23:01.974
<i>Until the day I can see you again</i>
